  {
    "sha": "8b850a18816e00d4ae1757c1de70b59e67cf3b84",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDhiODUwYTE4ODE2ZTAwZDRhZTE3NTdjMWRlNzBiNTllNjdjZjNiODQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:38:58Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:38:58Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): WCS page applies its origin from the footer beside Close, and says where the origin is\n\nThe WCS page's Set origin moves from the page body, among the quarter\nturns, to the fixed footer beside Close (egui_app::wcs_footer). While the\ntyped fields differ from the placed WCS, the footer shows \"Origin not\napplied\". Positions are compared to 1e-9 mm and angles as rotations.\n\nA new app::setup_origin says where the origin is, against the stock box\n(else the model's bounds): \"top of stock, front-left corner\", or signed\ndistances from the box's left side, front and top when it is on none of\nthe 27 anchor points. The page's header line and the setup sheet's new\norigin: line both read it.\n\ndocs/user-guide/work-origin.md explains where CamCraft shows the origin\nand how to change it.\n\nFixes #870\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
